#: ../../source/docs/common-parameter-reset.rst:5
#: 08a3d90004364b68a6d46ab8171fe4b9
msgid "Parameter Reset"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parameter-reset.rst:7
#: b5d79e9ed3784dd597ae3bbc90af308a
msgid "This article shows several ways to reset all parameters to their default values.If you would like to restore any of the existing setup parameters, save them to a file first!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parameter-reset.rst:11
#: b5ccb495f2e247c2970deb1468273fcc
msgid "Option #1: Using the Mission Planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parameter-reset.rst:13
#: 3d671ff5c3eb4fad8ef2880a8235cc00
msgid "Mission Planner has a dedicated **Reset to Default** button. This will reset all parameters to the vehicle's defaults."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parameter-reset.rst:15
#: b1bdc694134b4d009199706a9df92185
msgid "It will not reset the DroneCAN dynamic node address table. The other parameter reset methods listed below will also reset that table so that new devices can use previous addresses of devices that are being replaced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parameter-reset.rst:17
#: c49ba0d2696b416b9ced216d3ff7f2e3
msgid "Connect the autopilot to *Mission Planner*, and on the **CONFIG \\| Full Parameter List** or **Full Parameter Tree** page push the **Reset to Default** button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parameter-reset.rst:22
#: 9575a3bd449d41e9852b20f7883dc80c
msgid "The autopilot will automatically reboot, setting all parameters back to their default values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parameter-reset.rst:25
#: 2fb54e950ed049b28da7f70b7a6f2b8b
msgid "Option #2: Change the FORMAT_VERSION parameter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parameter-reset.rst:27
#: 9a659307a1cb4dd2884d365992d10b2e
msgid "On any Ground Control Station (that can write parameters) you can reset parameters by setting the :ref:`FORMAT_VERSION<FORMAT_VERSION>`  parameter to zero. After writing the parameter, reboot the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parameter-reset.rst:32
#: 6ac6191ecc8e4aa1880de1fa28840bac
msgid "Option #3: Load another vehicle's firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parameter-reset.rst:36
#: e8eae4d18d5c47708b18e5bbb0dd1435
msgid "This method is not recommended because it's unnecessarily time consuming."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parameter-reset.rst:39
#: 7f1ee857143f4ee3bd6c92ce4a60b362
msgid "Upload the firmware for a completely different vehicle type (I.e. if you were using Copter, now upload the Rover firmware).  Reboot the board and let it sit for 30 seconds to clear the EEPROM.  Then upload the original firmware (i.e. Copter) to the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parameter-reset.rst:46
#: b316c6109e3c4e83b86d9c99e9804bd3
msgid "Restoring Calibrations after Resets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parameter-reset.rst:48
#: ba44e6685e1f4de7958643c227c37f41
msgid "The above will also reset the flag used to indicate that Accelerometer and Compasses have been calibrated, so that even if you restore your old parameters from a file, the calibrations would still need to be repeated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parameter-reset.rst:50
#: 762ddddc3d18433690664e9977388886
msgid "There are two methods to allow these to be restored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parameter-reset.rst:52
#: d5868fb46d1e4bc29e155438d6c86801
msgid "**Only use this method if you are certain that the Accelerometer or Compass sensors have not changed in any manner since the parameters were stored in a file. Restoring inaccurate calibration data can lead to a crash!**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parameter-reset.rst:55
#: a98e85d8f1684af69ef2272c761d9cd6
msgid "Using Mission Planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parameter-reset.rst:57
#: e8a9aa3f116e4133af767455713bbed5
msgid "Press CTRL+F to get to advanced commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parameter-reset.rst:59
#: 55a3ea7271fc4ec997b272448baebfcd
msgid "Now restore your previously stored parameters (could have also been done as first step), which includes the calibration parameters, to the autopilot and reboot. Calibration should not be required to arm now."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parameter-reset.rst:61
#: 98c5b086b71240dd8a2ac3677186a882
msgid "Press the \"Force Accel Cal\" and/or \"Force Compass Cal\" to set the flag which indicates the cal has been done."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parameter-reset.rst:66
#: 6d91697d23b6475fa2a11b05dcf1fb55
msgid "Using MAVProxy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parameter-reset.rst:68
#: 7361daefab784a6bbf25bde77eefce50
msgid "Simply type \"forcecal\" will force the autopilot into a calibrated state. Be sure you have valid compass and IMU calibration values already loaded."
msgstr ""
